Yay, I finally ascended!

This game was a game I decided to try Dig for Victory on. There wasn't
much of a reason; I started with a digging wand, which is always
helpful, but nothing else useful for DfV (create monster spell,
polycontrol ring, +2 increase str ring, id scroll, light scroll, and a
couple of other things I can't remember).

Anyway, I had a pretty uneventful dig, having to Elbereth occasionally;
I had to use my wand of digging a few times, though, to escape the
titan on medusa, for one. I hit the castle about about dlvl 27, and
proceeded to head for the moat. I had picked up a couple of spells by
this point - drain life and remove curse, plus a wand of fire.

I had to avoid a Nazg=FAl as I made my way over, but then burned
Elbereth just outside the castle. I then proceeded to use the
drawbridge to crush most of the monsters inside, though an invisible
lich lurked (which I eventually, crushed). Oddly enough, there was a
hostile fire giant which refused to come over to attack me.

Somewhere near emptying the barracks, I accidentally force bolted the
drawbridge, trapping me inside, so I was forced inside the castle.
Luckily I found the wand at the first corner I looked in, wished up a
few things, then fled, jumping in the moat and climbing out the other
side. I wished for 2 blessed scrolls of charging, blessed gresed +2
SDSM, a +2 Helm of Brilliance (which came at +0), the blessed greased
master key of thievery (half damage, warning and TC was really nice),
and a blessed magic marker.

On the way up, I had problems with Medusa, first the stone golems +
cobras, then with the vampire lord following me across the water (I got
lev boots from perseus's statue, which I then uncursed). The vampire
also managed to drain a level through my CoMR, which was annoying, but
I was about level 11 then.

I eventually managed to make it across, and managed to make it to the
upstairs right as the titan summoned stuff at me. I fled up a few
levels, then found a level teleporter, and levelported to 1.

At this point, I had been using my tooled horn frequently, to scare
monsters. (Thanks, Grunt!).

>From this point, it was pretty standard; I sacrificed a ton of stuff
(create monster is a really useful spell), and got magicbane (and
ogresmasher...), bought a bunch of protection (I poly'd my cat, which I
retamed, into a blue dragon, after about 6 or 7 really stupid pets
(jackal, newt, gecko, yellow mold, etc)), and killed most of the
shopkeepers. Raiding a vault on the dig down helped, too. After a
while, I ended up with naked AC of -1, and ac of about -17 with armour
on.

I got a bunch of spells, scrolls, potions etc, and stashed pretty much
everything in sokoban (which contained an amulet of reflection. I'd
found a bag of holding somewhere along the lines).

At some point, I raided Fort Ludios, (the portal to which was at the
highest possible dungeon level), and turned nearly all the soldiers
into statues in one doorway. I still don't understand how that much
stuff can be on 1 space. So many statues, for one... 'trice corpses
rule. Croesus was wimpy.

The quest was easy; I breezed down to the Dark One, and killed him
pretty quickly. I didn't have see invisible, but warning from the MKoT
meant I could see him anyway.

I wrote a scroll of taming, confused myself, and tamed the stuff the
titan had summoned on medusa, and magic misiled it, then gated to soko
and polyed them into better pets (jabberwock, blue dragon, black
dragon, baby yellow dragon, baby green dragon, ice devil and purple
worm).

After a while (turn 40k?) I entered Gehennom, with spell of magic
missile, and used it to kill a lot of stuff (other notable spells were
polymorph, magic mapping, identify and finger of death).

Asmodeus read a cursed scroll of tele and vanished, I later found him
at the castle. The other demons were easy kills. I went about partway
down, then started forgetting some important spells, so gated back and
re-read some spellbooks. When I tele'd back down to the VotD, Yeenoghu
was somehow there (I had previously summoned him with same race
sacrifice, and hadn't revisited that level since). He was kinda
annoying, so I killed him too.

I can't remember much about this part of the game.

I went down in gehennom, then went back up to vlad, grabbing another
purple worm, and losing a bunch of other pets, and got the candelabrum.
I then went down and found the vibrating square (which was dlvl 49),
and left the candelabrum and bell there. Izchak only had 5 candles, but
I had 9 by that time.

I then went back, polyed a bunch of useless crap, got some good stuff,
lost a ton to shudderings.

I grabbed and decursed the water walking boots from vlads, and diluted
useless potions and scrolls, and wrote gold detection, amongst others,
got a bunch of holy water, and alchemised for 17 blessed full healing
potions. After reverse genociding nurses, quaffing 10 of those potions,
plus a few other potions, mainly a couple of gain level ones, and ended
with 300 max hp, from about 127. I was wearing the amulet of life
saving from vlad's, and with half spell damage and physical damage, I
essentially had 1200 hp... I also ended up with an AC of -41, naked AC
-3.

After this, I had an accident with forgetting to put my ring of
levitation back on and stepping into the water in jubilex's swamp, and
blanked a bunch of my scrolls, but I was fine with my equipment.

I went down, killed Rodney, (had blue dragon, black dragon and 4 purple
worms), levelported to the VS, performed the ritual, levelported to the
Sanctum, had rodney appear (which was somewhere near 20 turns after I
previously killed him), finger of death'd him again, grabbed the
amulet, and quaffed a potion of gain level.

I managed to leave a black dragon and 2 purple worms behind, then
grabbed my other dragon and worm (which were on a seperate level, and
managed to blow my magic whistle that time). The mysterious force
didn't seem to want to let me get above the wizard's tower, which was
annoying, as I couldn't even teleport to the stairs, but I managed to
get out. The wizard appeared on me again, and died again.

I reached experience level 23, as I had a couple of potions of gain
level, and a bunch of wraith corpses during the game.

Magicbane caught all the malignant black auras rodney sent down, though
I lost a purple worm to a slime from summoning. Though, I picked
another up on Jubilex's.

I left my blue dragon behind on the way up; can't remember why. It was
probably eating when I went up in gehennom, and I didn't want to tempt
the mysterious force even more.

Then, I went to the planes. I had detect monsters cast throughout, so
could see where everything was. Unfortunately, I had to leave about 75k
gold behind, as it was too heavy.  Earth was no problem; the portal was
near the middle, so a few dig wand charges got me there (out of the ~30
- 40 charges I had). I teleported stuff away a few times and a bunch of
monsters appeared when I was right next to the portal, so I used my
ring of conflict for the only time, and I had to kill a troll standing
right on it twice (I had to go pick up the amulet again, as I forget to
pick it up after dropping it to cast FoD a few times). I lost a purple
worm (... mk. V) here, as it was eating when I took the portal.

Air Plane was okay; I was engulfed a few times, and zapped death and
sleep wands at air elementals, and had little other trouble.

Fire plane was similarly okay. I was getting surrounded, but managed to
maneuver out of harms way. An archon spawned when I was partway to the
portal, but it didn't get close enough to do anything. I lost my last
remaining purple worm here (... mk. III); it died.

Water was again, okay - I had to use two scrolls of gold detection, but
was fine, ate until satiated, then went to Astral.

Astral was easy. Famine was left, Pesty middle, Death right. I went
left, tele'd stuff out the way, lit my lantern, FoD'd Famine, and
jumped to the altar, which was the right one, offered the amulet, and
ascended.

A few notes - I got polyselfless conduct, though early on I tried
polymorphing myself via a poly trap + poly control, but just got 'you
feel like a new elf'. I could've genocided h, but I chose not to. I
apparently had it extremely easy on the planes. I only had 9 luck,
which really surprised me; I was expecting it to be full. I had a
really lucky escape partway in - I had taken my stuff off to enchant my
HoB, when I black dragon breathed at me, when I had only got
disintegration resistance *very* shortly before. I actually had 4
potions of speed I intended to quaff for the planes, but completely
forgot about it. I could have actually managed to ascend without
increased my health from 127 to 300; I took hardly any damage on the
planes (about 250 or so was my lowest). I had a ring of regen I never
wore. I think either the stone golems on medusas were the monster that
did the most damage to me as a specific monster. Either that, or
Yeenoghu, which was partly because I was trying to Magic Missile him...
All thrones but one just vanished. Neferet the Green's healed me, and I
didn't try using it again. I was wearing leather gloves at the end,
despite finding gauntlets of power. I didn't like the hit to
spellcasting.

